{"slug":"/students/subjects/biology/foundations/cell-structure/","source":"students/subjects/biology/foundations/cell-structure.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Cell Structure - Biology","description":"","subject":"biology","body":"<!-- Header -->\n    <nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/biology-foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 mr-4\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Cell Structure</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-4\">\n                    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">\n                        Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-24 sm:w-32 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full\">\n                        <div id=\"progressBar\" class=\"h-2 bg-green-500 rounded-full transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Identify and describe the structure of plant and animal cells</li>\n                <li>• Explain the functions of key cell organelles</li>\n                <li>• Compare and contrast plant and animal cells</li>\n                <li>• Understand the Cell Theory and its importance</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Introduction to Cells -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                What is a Cell?\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A <strong>cell</strong> is the smallest structural and functional unit of life. All living organisms are made up of cells. Some organisms (like bacteria) are <strong>unicellular</strong> (single cell), while others (like humans) are <strong>multicellular</strong> (many cells).</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>The Cell Theory</h4>\n                <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li>All living things are composed of cells</li>\n                    <li>The cell is the basic unit of life</li>\n                    <li>All cells arise from pre-existing cells</li>\n                </ol>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\">Plant Cells</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Have a cell wall (cellulose)</li>\n                        <li>• Contain chloroplasts</li>\n                        <li>• Large permanent vacuole</li>\n                        <li>• Regular, fixed shape</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\">Animal Cells</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• No cell wall</li>\n                        <li>• No chloroplasts</li>\n                        <li>• Small temporary vacuoles</li>\n                        <li>• Irregular shape</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Cell Organelles -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Cell Organelles and Their Functions\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Each organelle has a specific function that helps the cell survive and perform its tasks. Here are the key organelles you need to know:</p>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <!-- Nucleus -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-blue-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Nucleus\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">The \"control center\" of the cell. Contains DNA (genetic material) and controls cell activities like growth, metabolism, and reproduction. Surrounded by a nuclear membrane with pores.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Mitochondria -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-orange-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Mitochondria\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">The \"powerhouse\" of the cell. Site of <strong>cellular respiration</strong> where glucose is broken down to release energy in the form of ATP. Has a double membrane with inner folds called cristae.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Ribosomes -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-pink-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-pink-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Ribosomes\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">Tiny structures that are the site of <strong>protein synthesis</strong>. Found free in cytoplasm or attached to endoplasmic reticulum. Made of RNA and protein.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Endoplasmic Reticulum -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-cyan-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-cyan-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER)\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\"><strong>Rough ER</strong> has ribosomes attached and transports proteins. <strong>Smooth ER</strong> has no ribosomes and makes lipids. Forms a network of membranes throughout the cell.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Golgi Apparatus -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-yellow-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-yellow-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Golgi Apparatus\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">The \"post office\" of the cell. Modifies, packages, and secretes proteins and lipids. Made of stacked, flattened membrane sacs called cisternae.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Cell Membrane -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-green-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Cell Membrane\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">A selectively permeable membrane that controls what enters and leaves the cell. Made of a <strong>phospholipid bilayer</strong> with embedded proteins. Protects the cell and maintains homeostasis.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Chloroplasts (Plant only) -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-emerald-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-emerald-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Chloroplasts (Plants Only)\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">Site of <strong>photosynthesis</strong> where sunlight is converted into food (glucose). Contains green pigment called chlorophyll. Has a double membrane with internal thylakoid membranes.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Cell Wall (Plant only) -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-amber-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Cell Wall (Plants Only)\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">A rigid outer layer made of <strong>cellulose</strong> that provides structural support and protection. Fully permeable to most substances. Gives plant cells their fixed shape.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Vacuole -->\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-violet-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 flex items-center\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -circle text-violet-500 mr-2 text-xs\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Vacuole\n                    </h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">Storage sac for water, nutrients, and waste. Plant cells have a large central vacuole that helps maintain <strong>turgor pressure</strong>. Animal cells have smaller, temporary vacuoles.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Interactive Diagram -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Interactive Cell Diagram\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Explore this interactive cell diagram to learn about different organelles. Click on each part to learn more!</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"simulation-container\" style=\"height: 550px;\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-builder/latest/area-builder_en.html\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Video Explanation -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Video: Introduction to Cells\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Watch this video for a comprehensive overview of cell structure:</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"video-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8IlzKri08kk\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Practice Problems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-green-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n                Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Which organelle is responsible for protein synthesis?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Ribosomes</strong> - They are the site where amino acids are assembled into proteins based on instructions from mRNA.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. State three differences between plant and animal cells.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n                                <li>Plant cells have a cell wall; animal cells do not</li>\n                                <li>Plant cells have chloroplasts; animal cells do not</li>\n                                <li>Plant cells have a large permanent vacuole; animal cells have small temporary vacuoles</li>\n                            </ol>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Why is the mitochondria called the \"powerhouse\" of the cell?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Mitochondria are called the \"powerhouse\" because they produce <strong>ATP (adenosine triphosphate)</strong> through cellular respiration. ATP is the energy currency of the cell, used for all cellular activities.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. What is the function of the cell membrane?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            The cell membrane:\n                            <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                                <li>Controls what enters and leaves the cell (selectively permeable)</li>\n                                <li>Protects the cell's internal environment</li>\n                                <li>Maintains homeostasis</li>\n                                <li>Contains receptors for cell signaling</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-green-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Cells are the basic unit of life - all living things are made of cells</li>\n                <li>• Plant and animal cells share many organelles but have key differences</li>\n                <li>• Each organelle has a specific function essential for cell survival</li>\n                <li>• The nucleus controls cell activities; mitochondria produce energy</li>\n                <li>• Plant cells uniquely have cell walls, chloroplasts, and large vacuoles</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Navigation -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/biology-foundations/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                <span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous\n            </a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/biology-topic-cell-properties/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-green-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-green-600\">\n                Next<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- Quiz Modal -->\n    <div id=\"quizModal\" class=\"hidden fixed inset-0 bg-gray-600 bg-opacity-50 overflow-y-auto h-full w-full z-50 p-4\">\n        <div class=\"relative top-10 md:top-20 mx-auto p-5 border w-full max-w-2xl shadow-lg rounded-md bg-white\">\n            <div id=\"quizContent\" class=\"p-4 md:p-6\"></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up {\n            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n        }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card {\n            background: white;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n        }\n        .simulation-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 500px;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .simulation-container iframe {\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }\n        .video-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .video-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }\n        .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n        .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}